.TH KERN 1 "2025-11-03" "kern" "System Monitoring Tool"
.SH NAME
kern \- real-time system monitoring tool with TUI and REST API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kern
[\-acdhmnvg] [\-\-ai] [\-\-mining] [\-\-refresh=\fISECONDS\fR] [\-l \fILANG\fR] [\-r \fIPORT\fR] [\-\-detailed]
.B kern
[\-\-api \fIURL\fR] [\-\-ssh \fIHOST\fR] [\-\-download-lang \fICODE\fR] [\-\-list-languages]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kern
is a comprehensive system monitoring tool that provides real-time information
about disk usage, CPU performance, memory utilization, network statistics,
GPU monitoring, AI training processes, and cryptocurrency mining activity.
It features a professional Terminal User Interface (TUI) with double buffering
to eliminate screen flickering, support for multiple languages with automatic
download, and multi-protocol remote monitoring via HTTP, HTTPS, and SSH.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Show all system information (default).
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-cpu
Show CPU information only.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-disk
Show disk information only.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message.
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-mem
Show memory information only.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-net
Show network information only.
.TP
.B \-g, \-\-gpu
Show GPU information only (requires NVIDIA or AMD drivers).
.TP
.B \-\-ai
Show AI training information only.
.TP
.B \-\-mining
Show cryptocurrency mining information only.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show version information and logo.
.TP
.B \-\-refresh=\fISECONDS\fR
Set refresh interval in seconds (default: 2).
.TP
.B \-l \fILANG\fR
Set interface language. Use \-\-list-languages to see all supported codes.
.TP
.B \-r \fIPORT\fR
Start remote API server on specified port (default: 28126).
.TP
.B \-\-detailed
Show detailed CPU core information (individual core usage).
.TP
.B \-\-api \fIURL\fR
Monitor remote server via HTTP/HTTPS API.
.TP
.B \-\-ssh \fIHOST\fR
Monitor remote server via SSH.
.TP
.B \-\-download-lang \fICODE\fR
Download language pack for specified language code.
.TP
.B \-\-list-languages
List all supported language codes.
.TP
.B \-\-logo
Show application logo during monitoring.
.SH TUI CONTROLS
When running in interactive mode, the following controls are available:
.TP
.B q, Q, ESC
Quit the application
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Quit the application
.TP
.B Terminal Resize
Interface automatically adapts to terminal size changes
.SH REMOTE MONITORING
.B kern
supports multiple remote monitoring protocols:
.TP
.B HTTP/HTTPS API
REST API accessible via HTTP or HTTPS (with TLS termination)
.TP
.B SSH
Direct SSH execution or SSH tunneling
.TP
.B Local Network
Access within local network segments
.TP
.B Global Internet
Access via public IP with port forwarding
.SH API
When started with the
.B \-r
option,
.B kern
provides a REST API on the specified port (28126 by default):
.TP
.B GET /api/cpu
Returns JSON with CPU information.
.TP
.B GET /api/mem
Returns JSON with memory information.
.TP
.B GET /api/disk
Returns JSON with disk information.
.TP
.B GET /api/net
Returns JSON with network information.
.TP
.B GET /api/gpu
Returns JSON with GPU information.
.TP
.B GET /api/ai
Returns JSON with AI training information.
.TP
.B GET /api/mining
Returns JSON with mining information.
.TP
.B GET /api/system
Returns JSON with system information.
.TP
.B GET /health
Returns health status.
.PP
Example usage:
.IP
kern -r 28126
.br
curl http://localhost:28126/api/cpu
.br
kern --api http://192.168.1.100:28126
.SH GPU MONITORING
GPU monitoring requires:
.IP \(bu 3
NVIDIA GPUs: nvidia-smi utility (included with NVIDIA drivers)
.IP \(bu 3
AMD GPUs: rocm-smi utility (included with ROCm)
.PP
GPU monitoring provides:
.IP \(bu 3
Temperature and utilization metrics
.IP \(bu 3
Memory usage (VRAM)
.IP \(bu 3
Power consumption and clock speeds
.IP \(bu 3
Fan speed and performance state
.SH AI TRAINING MONITORING
AI training detection monitors for:
.IP \(bu 3
TensorFlow, PyTorch, Keras, and HuggingFace processes
.IP \(bu 3
VRAM usage by AI frameworks
.IP \(bu 3
Training metrics (loss, accuracy, throughput)
.IP \(bu 3
Batch size and epoch information
.SH MINING MONITORING
Mining detection identifies:
.IP \(bu 3
Popular mining software (xmrig, ethminer, t-rex, etc.)
.IP \(bu 3
Mining algorithms (RandomX, Ethash, SHA-256)
.IP \(bu 3
Hashrate and share statistics
.IP \(bu 3
Power efficiency and profitability estimates
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B q, Q, ESC
Quit the application.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B kern
Monitor all system resources with default settings.
.TP
.B kern \-d \-m
Monitor only disk and memory usage.
.TP
.B kern \-\-refresh=5 \-l ru
Update every 5 seconds with Russian interface.
.TP
.B kern \-\-detailed
Show detailed CPU core information.
.TP
.B kern \-g \-\-ai
Monitor GPU and AI training processes.
.TP
.B kern \-\-mining
Monitor cryptocurrency mining activity.
.TP
.B kern \-r
Start remote API server on default port 28126.
.TP
.B kern \-r 26001
Start remote API server on custom port 26001.
.TP
.B kern \-\-api http://192.168.1.100:28126
Monitor remote server via HTTP API.
.TP
.B kern \-\-api https://monitoring.example.com:28126
Monitor remote server via HTTPS API.
.TP
.B kern \-\-ssh user@remote\-host
Monitor remote server via SSH.
.TP
.B kern \-\-download\-lang fr
Download French language pack.
.TP
.B kern \-\-list\-languages
List all supported languages.
.TP
.B kern \-\-logo
Show application logo during monitoring.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kern/kern.json
Configuration file storing user preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.config/kern/i18n/
Directory containing downloaded language packs.
.TP
.I /usr/local/share/kern/i18n/
System directory containing language files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, 1 on error.
